 @mikerzisu9508  I understand your point, I (as others pointed) feel the fanboy comment was unnecessary. Expecting competence (not even excellence) from a hardware/software vendor should be the minimum. And yes I owned AIW Radeon cards back in the day and they crashed a lot. They also did stuff that no nvidia cards did with respect to capture and TV tuner and so forth. ATI was the jack of all trades, nvidia was the master of gaming. But all that was easy compared to the days of having to set XMS/EMS memory profiles to run games on 4MB of RAM.

The question is - is Intel going to be supporting Arc in 5 years. Else it will become a paperweight relative to AMD's fine wine and Nvidia's competent drivers. Sounds like a lot of the tech industry questions that.

BTW I still have an Intel camera from circa 2000 - 1.2MP. It stopped getting support after just 2 years.
